|**Development / vendors**                               |Provide supported telemetry and diagnostic interfaces, diagnose defects, correct code, improve application behavior, test fixes, and disclose support constraints.                                              |Instrumentation, supported fixes, product documentation, test evidence, and defect-resolution commitments.                |
|**Infrastructure / platform / database / network teams**|Operate and recover their components. Own configuration, patching, backups, component capacity, redundancy, and infrastructure improvements.                                                                    |Component recovery, change records, capacity evidence, and tested backup/restore or failover capabilities.                |
|**Monitoring engineering**                              |Maintain monitoring tools and MoM integrations, service models, dashboards, rules, correlation, routing, and telemetry quality. Own configuration lifecycle and assign a named MoM platform owner.              |Working integrations, service-health views, actionable alerts, routing configuration, and monitoring-platform reliability.|
|**Command-center operators**                            |Watch dashboards, acknowledge alerts, qualify impact, create/update incidents, engage resolvers, execute approved first-response procedures, track progress, and verify recovery signals.                       |Qualified incidents, accepted assignments, escalation records, shift handovers, and monitoring evidence.                  |
|**Designated incident manager**                         |Coordinate major incidents, appoint response roles, manage communications, escalate delays or conflicts, and maintain the decision log. This role may sit within the command center.                            |Incident command, coordinated workstreams, stakeholder updates, and major-incident closure records.                       |
|**ITSM practice / problem owner**                       |Maintain practice rules, assure record quality, coordinate problem investigation, track corrective actions, and verify closure criteria.                                                                        |Incident/problem governance, known-error records, action tracking, and evidence-based problem closure.                    |
