The service owner and business representative may be the same person where authority and responsibilities are explicitly assigned. They do not need to be separate departments.

During a major incident, appoint a technical lead in addition to the incident manager. The technical lead coordinates diagnosis and recovery across resolver teams. Google distinguishes incident command, communications, and operations roles. 3

4. Distribution of SRE practices

The following matrix assigns one accountable role for each defined activity. Contributors retain responsibility for completing their assigned work.

|Practice / activity                                 |Accountable role                          |Execution across teams                                                                                                                       |Required evidence                                                                      |
|----------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|**Approve service-level objectives**                |Service owner                             |Business identifies outcomes; SRE designs indicators and measurement; technical teams confirm feasibility.                                   |SLI/SLO specification: scope, calculation, target, window, data source, and exclusions.|
|**Apply the error-budget policy**                   |Service owner                             |SRE reports consumption and causes; business and technical owners prioritize actions; engineering/vendors implement fixes.                   |Agreed decision policy, reliability report, and funded corrective actions.             |
|**Implement SLI and error-budget measurement**      |SRE lead for an accepted engagement       |Monitoring implements data collection; application/infrastructure teams supply telemetry; SRE validates calculations.                        |Reproducible calculations, data-quality checks, and reviewed results.                  |
|**Maintain monitoring and alert configuration**     |Monitoring engineering lead               |SRE advises on reliability signals; technical teams validate symptoms; command center supplies operational feedback.                         |Tested rules, dashboards, service mappings, routing, and runbooks.                     |
|**Operate the alert queue**                         |Command-center shift lead                 |Operators acknowledge, qualify, route, escalate, and maintain handover.                                                                      |Accepted assignments, timely escalation, and complete operational records.             |
|**Coordinate a major incident**                     |Designated incident manager               |Command center maintains coordination; technical leads direct recovery; SRE/vendors join as required.                                        |Response roles, decision log, communications, and recovery evidence.                   |
|**Restore a failed component**                      |Affected technical domain owner           |Application support, infrastructure, development/vendor, or other resolver executes recovery within authority.                               |Validated recovery and recorded actions.                                               |
|**Complete incident learning and problem follow-up**|Named problem owner                       |All responding teams contribute; SRE examines systemic issues; technical owners implement corrections.                                       |Blameless review, owned actions, verification, and justified closure.                  |
|**Deliver SRE-owned automation**                    |SRE engineering lead                      |Operators identify toil; technical owners assist with implementation; operating teams validate usability.                                    |Tested automation, maintainer, operating procedure, and measured benefit.              |
|**Plan service capacity and performance**           |Service owner                             |Business supplies demand; SRE coordinates service analysis; technical teams and vendors test limits and implement changes.                   |Demand model, bottleneck evidence, tested headroom, and investment decisions.          |
|**Validate resilience and recovery**                |Continuity / DR authority for the exercise|SRE identifies failure scenarios; technical teams test; application support validates functionality; command center coordinates where needed.|Recovery results against approved objectives and owned remediation.                    |
|**Authorize a production change**                   |Change authority                          |Implementing teams supply test and rollback evidence; SRE contributes reliability findings; monitoring observes results.                     |Authorization, rollback/stop criteria, and execution conditions.                       |
|**Accept production readiness**                     |Service owner                             |SRE reviews reliability where engaged; every operating team proves its responsibilities are deliverable.                                     |Readiness assessment, operational acceptance, and documented residual risks.           |

Where SRE is not engaged, explicitly assign measurement and reliability-engineering duties to a named technical owner. Central monitoring does not automatically establish SRE support obligations.

