11. Reusable onboarding record

Use one record per business service. Link to existing authoritative records rather than duplicating them where possible.

|Field             |Value / evidence to supply                                                               |
|------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Service identity  |Service ID, name, purpose, environment, catalog link.                                    |
|Business context  |Business owner, critical journeys, operating periods, criticality, impact.               |
|Accountability    |Named service owner and accountable technical owners.                                    |
|Support           |Resolver groups, coverage, primary/backup contacts, vendor entitlement, escalation.      |
|Dependencies      |Maintained map and relevant component/entity identifiers.                                |
|Reliability       |SLI definitions, targets, windows, data sources, exclusions, error-budget policy.        |
|Monitoring sources|Tools, connector owners, data access, data freshness, diagnostic links.                  |
|Event behavior    |Identity, severity mapping, lifecycle, deduplication, correlation, maintenance rules.    |
|Response          |Runbooks, incident integration, communications, recovery and closure criteria.           |
|Readiness evidence|Acceptance-test results, operator handover, functional recovery validation.              |
|SRE engagement    |Scope, engineering responsibilities, incident triggers, coverage, and support acceptance.|
|Outstanding risks |Risk description, owner, acceptance authority, remediation, and review point.            |
|Approval          |Service owner and accepting operational/engineering team representatives.                |

